    "pfs_status_raw": null,
    "sections_raw": [
      {
        "heading_raw": null,
        "body_raw": "The warded creature or object becomes difficult to detect by divination spells such as clairaudience/clairvoyance, locate object, and detect spells. Nondetection also prevents location by such magic items as crystal balls. If a divination is attempted against the warded creature or item, the caster of the divination must succeed on a caster level check (1d20 + caster level) against a DC of 11 + the caster level of the spellcaster who cast nondetection. If you cast nondetection on yourself or on an item currently in your possession, the DC is 15 + your caster level.\n\nIf cast on a creature, nondetection wards the creature’s gear as well as the creature itself.\n\nNondetection, Communal\nSource: PRG:UC\n\nLevel antipaladin 4, mesmerist 4, occultist 4, psychic 4, sorcerer/wizard 4\nComponents V, S, M (diamond dust worth 25 gp per target)\nTarget creatures or objects touched"
      }
    ]
